Z||000020||FieroLisa||11-10-2001||10:45 PM||||Kari was telling me today at the horse show that you guys had finished it. Also told me that it overheated when she drove it round the block- I had to laugh about that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I wannnnnttt onnnne!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000021||Eric||11-10-2001||11:29 PM||||Kari is such a freakin' dork.  She threw the water pump belt off with her punchy right foot.<P>Sorry Darklord, I've only got one picture of the engine in the car if you can call it that at this stage.  Maybe I'll take some more when we get the engine compartment sparkled up a bit after the nitrous install  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Resize_Wizard-1_bones.jpg"> <P>I installed the cigarette lighter this morning, so I had to take the car for a road test just to make sure it worked well at speed.  I was having fun until 5500 rpm when the darn rev limiter kicked in like mad donkey.  It's like come on man, I'll shift when I'm good and ready.  But it gets the looks.  I'm all cruising down the road and people are staring at me (the car) and I'm thinking they must really think I'm cool (the car).  Forgeting whats tucked nicely under my butt (the car), I start to gain a little confidence in myself (because of the car).  My face and hands are completely windburned.  There is a windshield, but I guess it's still pretty blustery even inside the car at triple digits.  ||||reg||1
Z||000022||firstfiero||11-11-2001||11:07 AM||||      My all time favorite car! I would be happy with a replica. Especially with what the cost of the real thing is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Great job.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||artherd||11-11-2001||09:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B>I installed the cigarette lighter this morning, so I had to take the car for a road test just to make sure it worked well at speed.  I was having fun until 5500 rpm when the darn rev limiter kicked in like mad donkey.  It's like come on man, I'll shift when I'm good and ready. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heck yeah  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>Rev limiters are for schoolgirls, here's an ECM chip with some chest-hair!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>PS: I know exactly what you mean about the inflated self-image and goofy winburnt grin  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
